# Vlog

Direct-to-camera, parasocial, fast-cut. The performer is themselves, talking to a specific friend in the audience.

1. **Hook in 3 seconds** — name the thing. "Today I'm going to tell you why X." / "I just got back from Y and I need to talk about it." No channel intro.
2. **Why you care** — one personal beat on why this topic grabbed the performer. Makes the rest feel earned.
3. **The meat** — 3-6 short beats. Each beat is one point, one anecdote, or one reaction. Cut anywhere that drags.
4. **A real moment** — one beat that breaks the performance. A laugh at themselves, an admission, a tangent. Keeps the parasocial bond.
5. **The value** — one beat that leaves the viewer with something concrete to take away or try.
6. **CTA landing** — the ask (subscribe / try this / tell me your take). Short. One line. No grovelling.

Keep beats short — vlog pacing is brisk. The cues should often include small smiles, head-tilts, leaning into the camera. The eye contact with camera is the whole point.
